    "details": {
      "biography": {
        "value": "<p><strong>Tobias Wren</strong> has lodged in room 6 (206 on the Foundry map) for 43 years and disputes the bill because his body was replaced. He is gentle, sad, with an excellent memory for detail. He talks to a chair: the old body's favourite chair.</p><p><strong>GM notes (Quest 3, 'The Man in Room 6').</strong> <em>Insight DC 11:</em> he is not lying. He feels like a different man and is also the same one. <em>'The old body wore out. The new one fits badly. I remember everything. That's the problem. I remember it as someone else.'</em> A <strong>bone tag</strong> under a floorboard (Perception DC 12) is his original identity anchor. The twist: the custody ledger shows the body was at a licensed restoration house for six years, so those years are custody costs, not lodging. Reward: his <strong>stamped referral card</strong>, handed over in person, and the advice <em>'They will ask for the name three times. Bring the name.'</em> Backstory (suggested): <em>'Three graveyards. All three tended the same week. The tenders never spoke, but they left each other bread.'</em></p>",
        "public": ""
      },
      "alignment": "neutral good",
